# The default Flatpaks. Installed system-wide, once: by
# pulsar-flatpaks.service on the first boot that has a network, or by
# `sudo pulsar setup apps` if you would rather watch it happen. After that
# first success the service never runs again, so removing an app on a
# running system sticks -- this list is a starting set, not enforced state.
#
# FORMAT: one application ID per line, optionally followed by the remote to
# install it from. The remote defaults to `flathub` when the column is
# omitted, so every line that predates the second column still means what it
# always did. Both remotes are shipped as /etc/flatpak/remotes.d files.
#
# ORDER MATTERS on a bad network. The script installs top to bottom and a run
# that dies halfway leaves no stamp and retries, so the set that makes the
# desktop usable at all is listed FIRST and the gaming stack second. A user
# staring at a half-installed first boot should be looking at a machine that
# has a text editor.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The stock Silverblue desktop.
#
# Pulsar is Silverblue+, so this is the + being honest about the base it
# claims. These are the 18 applications a Fedora Silverblue ISO installs by
# default, from the same `fedora` remote it uses.
#
# They are listed rather than inherited because they CANNOT be inherited: the
# Silverblue container ships /var empty and configures no remotes, so Fedora's
# defaults exist only in the Anaconda payload of Fedora's own ISO. See
# etc/flatpak/remotes.d/fedora.flatpakrepo for the whole story. Nothing here
# is a Pulsar opinion -- it is the base, restored.
#
# Nautilus, Firefox and Software are absent on purpose: those three are RPMs
# in the Silverblue image and are already installed.
org.gnome.TextEditor            fedora
org.gnome.Calculator            fedora
org.gnome.Loupe                 fedora
org.gnome.Papers                fedora
org.gnome.NautilusPreviewer     fedora
org.gnome.Calendar              fedora
org.gnome.Contacts              fedora
org.gnome.clocks                fedora
org.gnome.Weather               fedora
org.gnome.Maps                  fedora
org.gnome.Snapshot              fedora
org.gnome.Characters            fedora
org.gnome.font-viewer           fedora
org.gnome.baobab                fedora
org.gnome.Logs                  fedora
org.gnome.Connections           fedora
org.gnome.Extensions            fedora
org.fedoraproject.MediaWriter   fedora

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The + .
#
# Curation rules: the launchers and daily drivers a fresh install is actually
# missing, nothing Microsoft-owned, nothing an average boot does not use.

# launchers -- the out-of-box gap between a fresh image and a playable one
com.valvesoftware.Steam
io.github.Faugus.faugus-launcher

# plumbing -- proton management, sandbox permissions, wine prefixes
com.vysp3r.ProtonPlus
com.github.tchx84.Flatseal
com.usebottles.bottles

# daily drivers
com.discordapp.Discord
com.obsproject.Studio
com.github.wwmm.easyeffects
